<template><article class="st-prose"><p class="atlas-eyebrow">About SectorTrace</p><h1>Evidence for the substance misuse sector</h1><p>SectorTrace collects published evidence about England's drug and alcohol treatment sector. It supports research into providers, commissioning, public funding, workforce conditions and treatment activity.</p><h2>Campaign origins</h2><p>The project began as an evidence base for a trade union pay campaign. Its public research tools serve a wider sector audience. Published campaign statements are labelled with their authorship, citations and limitations.</p><h2>Reading the evidence</h2><p>Each source describes a particular population and period. Pay, funding, treatment and legal records remain separate. Missing evidence does not establish that an event never occurred, and missing values are never treated as zero.</p><p>Source controls show the metadata available for an observation. Some public responses have less detail than others. SectorTrace does not supply a composite provider score.</p><div class="atlas-actions"><NuxtLink to="/coverage" class="atlas-button">Evidence coverage</NuxtLink><NuxtLink to="/catalogue" class="atlas-button">Dataset catalogue</NuxtLink><NuxtLink to="/api" class="atlas-button">Public API</NuxtLink></div></article></template>
